    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, that's a good start. It's a bit too formal for my relationship with my boss, though. He's pretty chill, so we can be a little more direct. Can you make it sound less like a template and more like a real person talking? Also, can you add a section that specifically emphasizes how these \"unplanned requirements\" are essentially sneaking in and eating up our dev time without us noticing until it's too late?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Subject: Need to Talk About Our Project\n\nHey [Boss's Name],\n\nHope you're doing well. I've been keeping an eye on our current project, and it's starting to feel like we're playing a never-ending game of Whack-a-Mole with scope creep. Every time we think we've got a handle on things, new requirements pop up, and it's like they're gobbling up our dev time without us even noticing until we're left with a mountain of work and no time to breathe.\n\nI know we're all committed to delivering top-notch software, but I'm starting to worry that we're stretching ourselves too thin. It's like we're trying to fit a whole new set of tools into our toolbox without any extra space. We need to either bring in more hands to help us out or give ourselves some extra time to finish what we've got.\n\nI don't want to sound like I'm complaining, but I think it's important to address this now before it starts to affect the quality of our work or our team's morale. Let's chat about how we can tackle this issue together and keep our project on track.\n\nLooking forward to hearing your thoughts.\n\nBest,\n[Your Name]",
      "source": "target",
