      "content": "Subject: Whack-a-Mole Project Update\n\nHey [Boss's Name],\n\nHope all's good on your end. I've been keeping an eye on our project, and it's starting to feel like we're playing a never-ending game of Whack-a-Mole with scope creep. Every time we think we've got a handle on things, new requirements pop up, and it's like they're gobbling up our dev time without us even noticing until we're left with a mountain of work and no time to breathe.\n\nIt's almost like these unplanned requirements are tiny, invisible forces working against us. They sneak in like little goblins, popping up out of nowhere and slowly undermining our progress. It's like they're playing a game of hide and seek with our time and resources, and we're the ones getting caught off guard every time.\n\nI know we're all committed to delivering top-notch software, but I'm starting to worry that we're stretching ourselves too thin. It's like we're trying to fit a whole new set of tools into our toolbox without any extra space. We need to either bring in more hands to help us out or give ourselves some extra time to finish what we've got.\n\nI don't want to sound like I'm complaining, but I think it's important to address this now before it starts",
